title: Paradigm as A* — reliable traversal, not perfect optimality
summary: Paradigm is the A* of development methodology. Not theoretically optimal in every case, but a tried-and-true traversal algorithm that reliably yields good results when followed. The symbol system, .purpose files, gates, flows, and stop hooks are the heuristic — imperfect but bounded. Any team can adopt it and get results if they follow the course, even when the system feels arcane at first.
